// "[Permanent] connives" [CR#701.50a]: that permanent's controller draws a
// card, then discards a card, and puts a +1/+1 counter on the conniving
// permanent if a nonland card is discarded this way. That is connive N's
// process for one card (`conniveN(1)`, [CR#701.50d]), so the body is that
// declaration's, and its deed is the one event either form makes
// [CR#701.50f]: `connive` names no deed of its own (`deed: None`), or bare
// connive would enact twice.
KeywordAction(
    name: "connive",
    params: [],
    spelling: "connive",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "connive",
        frame_set: Intransitive,
    ),
    deed: None,
    body: conniveN(1),
)
